WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:08.550
King Arthur followed Merlin the magician into the shadows of the forest.

2
00:00:08.551 --> 00:00:10.668
It was tranquil and beautiful.

3
00:00:10.669 --> 00:00:13.190
"Where are we going?" Arthur asked.

4
00:00:13.191 --> 00:00:16.834
"To the lake, my king," answered Merlin.

5
00:00:16.835 --> 00:00:20.690
"Will I find my sword there?" asked the king.

6
00:00:20.691 --> 00:00:25.830
Merlin did not answer. He stopped when they reached the lake.

7
00:00:25.831 --> 00:00:28.829
The king stood and looked at the calm waters.

8
00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.984
Arthur had never seen such a beautiful lake in his life.

9
00:00:32.985 --> 00:00:37.308
"This is an enchanted lake, my lord," explained Merlin.

10
00:00:37.309 --> 00:00:40.254
Suddenly the waters began to move.

11
00:00:40.255 --> 00:00:44.015
Then from the center of the lake appeared a woman's arm.

12
00:00:44.016 --> 00:00:49.438
She was holding a magnificent and grand sword.

13
00:00:49.439 --> 00:00:52.340
The sword shone brightly in the sun.

14
00:00:52.341 --> 00:00:58.738
"Behold Excalibur, my lord. That is the name of the sword." Merlin pointed.

15
00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:02.142
"Excalibur," repeated Arthur with awe.

16
00:01:02.143 --> 00:01:04.965
He stood up and walked toward the lake.

17
00:01:04.966 --> 00:01:11.794
"Wait, my lord, it is not as easy as that," Merlin warned.

18
00:01:11.795 --> 00:01:15.528
"The lady of the lake holds Excalibur in her hand.

19
00:01:15.529 --> 00:01:18.865
She will only give the sword to its rightful owner.

20
00:01:18.866 --> 00:01:23.165
Many brave knights have tried to claim Excalibur for themselves.

21
00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:25.108
All of them have failed.

22
00:01:25.109 --> 00:01:29.851
They failed because Excalibur was not their sword."

23
00:01:29.852 --> 00:01:35.016
"But I will not fail, for my heart tells me I am the owner of that great sword."

24
00:01:35.017 --> 00:01:38.039
Arthur knew Excalibur belonged to him.

25
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.748
As he reached out and touched the handle, the lady let go of Excalibur.

26
00:01:42.749 --> 00:01:47.326
Then her arm disappeared beneath the waves.

27
00:01:47.327 --> 00:01:52.360
"In my hand I hold the most beautiful sword in the world, Excalibur!

28
00:01:52.361 --> 00:01:56.519
Excalibur will make England the mightiest country in history!

29
00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:01.455
It will make me the greatest king in the world!" Arthur proclaimed.

30
00:02:01.456 --> 00:02:04.664
King Arthur won many battles with Excalibur.

31
00:02:04.665 --> 00:02:10.947
As he had promised, England became the most powerful country in the world.

32
00:02:10.948 --> 00:02:15.812
King Arthur continued to fight and conquer all of England's enemies.

33
00:02:15.813 --> 00:02:18.625
However, there was trouble in Camelot.

34
00:02:18.626 --> 00:02:26.192
While Arthur was away fighting with Excalibur, Queen Guinevere fell in love with Arthur's best friend Lancelot.

35
00:02:26.193 --> 00:02:30.425
When Arthur found out, he became very angry.

36
00:02:30.426 --> 00:02:36.958
Lancelot was forced into hiding, and Guinevere was thrown into prison by Arthur's guards.

37
00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:41.184
Problems also arose among the knights of King Arthur's Round Table.

38
00:02:41.185 --> 00:02:43.740
The knights began to have disagreements.

39
00:02:43.741 --> 00:02:50.043
Some of them became enemies, and the society of the Round Table came to an end.

40
00:02:50.044 --> 00:02:53.742
Soon after, England began to lose its battles.

41
00:02:53.743 --> 00:02:57.443
Many soldiers were killed or taken as captives.

42
00:02:57.444 --> 00:03:02.290
England needed its king, but Arthur was away on a different battle.

43
00:03:02.291 --> 00:03:06.647
He was searching for Lancelot in order to kill him.

44
00:03:06.648 --> 00:03:13.167
King Arthur had a son named Mordred, but Mordred did not like his father and had an evil heart.

45
00:03:13.168 --> 00:03:15.688
He wanted to become the king of England.

46
00:03:15.689 --> 00:03:22.112
Mordred knew his father had become weak, so Mordred set off to capture and kill his father.

47
00:03:22.113 --> 00:03:26.809
After many days, Mordred found his father.

48
00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:30.380
"What brings you here, my son?" Arthur asked.

49
00:03:30.381 --> 00:03:36.087
"I have come to claim the throne as king of England," answered Mordred.

50
00:03:36.088 --> 00:03:38.782
"But I am still the king," said Arthur.

51
00:03:38.783 --> 00:03:42.444
"Not for long," said Mordred.

52
00:03:42.445 --> 00:03:48.639
Back in Camelot, Merlin the magician sensed that something terrible was going to happen.

53
00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:52.027
England was losing its battles.

54
00:03:52.028 --> 00:03:55.556
Now the king and his son were fighting against each other.

55
00:03:55.557 --> 00:03:57.681
Merlin thought about Excalibur.

56
00:03:57.682 --> 00:04:04.633
He knew Excalibur was a special sword, but he also knew Excalibur had caused much pain and death.

57
00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:08.176
"Excalibur should never have left the lake.

58
00:04:08.177 --> 00:04:13.064
That is where it belongs," Merlin said to himself.

59
00:04:13.065 --> 00:04:17.516
After his battle with his son, King Arthur rode back to the forest.

60
00:04:17.517 --> 00:04:19.924
He did not want to fight anymore.

61
00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:25.246
He had lost all his friends, his wife, and now even his son was dead.

62
00:04:25.247 --> 00:04:28.310
He looked at Excalibur with dismay.

63
00:04:28.311 --> 00:04:32.336
Arthur threw Excalibur high into the air above the lake.

64
00:04:32.337 --> 00:04:39.603
As it fell toward the surface, suddenly the lady's arm appeared from the water.

65
00:04:39.604 --> 00:04:46.788
She caught Excalibur in her hand and held it for a moment shining brightly and beautifully in the sun.

66
00:04:46.789 --> 00:04:50.189
Then it disappeared into the lake forever.

67
00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:53.689
No one knows what happened to King Arthur after that.

68
00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:58.009
Some believe King Arthur will return when England needs him again.

69
00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:03.574
Whatever may happen, the legend of King Arthur lives on.
